FACTORY AUDIT REPORTS
Last three audit reports for Factory K (FAC-0001, Law Knitting 1, supplier SUP-0001)
Location: Tiruppur, Tamil Nadu, India

AUDIT 1 (AUD-900001, about twelve weeks ago, social audit, grade B)
Finding: Overtime records incomplete for one week - raised, then CLOSED after the factory sent a corrected timesheet
Finding: Piece-rate wage calculation documentation missing for 5 workers - CLOSED once the factory produced the records
Finding: Fire exits - no issue recorded

AUDIT 2 (AUD-900002, about five weeks ago, social audit, grade B)
Finding: Overtime records still incomplete, same issue as Audit 1 - REOPENED (repeat issue)
Finding: Fire exit blocked by stored materials; sprinkler maintenance overdue - OPEN (new)
Finding: Wage calculation documentation now complete - stayed CLOSED

AUDIT 3 (AUD-900003, about one week ago, ethical audit, grade C)
Finding: Excessive overtime not compensated properly; 60+ hour weeks without breaks - REOPENED again (repeat, third audit in a row)
Finding: Fire exits still blocked and no emergency procedures; same finding as Audit 2 not actioned - REOPENED (repeat issue)
Finding: Gender-based wage discrimination in the piece-rate system - OPEN (new, major)
Finding: Wage calculation records remain complete - CLOSED

AUDIT FINDINGS ANALYSIS:
- Closed issues that came back: overtime records (closed after Audit 1, back in Audits 2 and 3) and fire exits (back in Audit 3 after being raised in Audit 2).
- Wage calculation documentation did not come back; it is the one issue that stayed closed.
- Repeat findings across three audits with grades B, B, C point to a weak management system: corrective actions are closed on paperwork without verification of the fix.
- Suggested next audit focus: overtime and working hours records against payroll, fire exits and emergency procedures, and the piece-rate pay system.
